  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the hateful textual message",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'the floor is jews' because the meme's intent is to make the viewer identify with or internalize the hateful stereotype being conveyed. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the meme's structure and overall intent create an implicit projection where the viewer is positioned as the one who is 'on the floor' — metaphorically and literally — by the antisemitic message. The user is thus projected onto the text_chunk as the target of the hate speech and the implied subject of the metaphor.",
